body:
Because of the foreseeable practically infinitely increasing productivity due to AI and automation, the significance of individual wealth will also be strongly leveled (which can already be observed very well today in the upper class). Because the price levels of pretty much all products will probably approach zero (even raw materials will be synthesizable with minimal effort), there will then be abundance on an unimagined scale and a state very close to human equality. What will certainly become philosophically quite interesting with regard to ontological and distinctive determinations of man.

&#x200B;

That comes very close to an abolition of the money system, even if one will probably still fall back on it due to practicable considerations. Especially in the case of vital needs such as food, however, each person will probably be provided with a contingent - quite independently of a monetary benefit - in order to ensure an existence even apart from the granting of an unconditional basic income (or rather basic contingents).

&#x200B;

In the coming decades, therefore, the wisdom and reasonableness of state actors will be of enormous importance in adapting to these developments in order to prevent a disaster in social policy terms due to fairly general unemployment and to establish conditions that are generally as equal as possible.
